{"bill":{"id":"119-sjres-115","congress":119,"billType":"sjres","billNumber":"115","title":"A joint resolution to direct the removal of United States Armed Forces from hostilities within or against the Islamic Republic of Iran that have not been authorized by Congress.","introducedDate":"2026-03-05","latestActionDate":"2026-03-05","latestActionText":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Foreign Relations.","policyArea":"International Affairs","subjects":[],"sponsorBioguideId":"M001169","cosponsorBioguideIds":["B001288","K000384","S001150","S000148","K000377","K000394"],"committeeCodes":[],"committeeNames":[],"officialSummary":"This joint resolution directs the President to remove U.S. Armed Forces from hostilities within or against Iran unless a declaration of war or authorization to use military force for such purpose has been enacted. The resolution specifies that it shall not be construed to prevent the United States from defending against an attack on the United States or its personnel or facilities in other nations.","congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-joint-resolution/115","source":"congress","sourceUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/sjres/BILLSTATUS-119sjres115.xml","fetchedAt":"2026-07-29T01:30:28.355Z"},"classification":{"billId":"119-sjres-115","plainSummary":"This joint resolution would require the President to withdraw U.S. military forces from any hostilities in or against Iran unless Congress has formally declared war or passed specific authorization for such military action. The measure includes an exception allowing the U.S. to defend itself and its personnel or facilities abroad if attacked. It addresses the scope of presidential authority to conduct military operations without explicit congressional approval.","industries":[{"industry":"defense","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"The resolution directly governs deployment and use of U.S. Armed Forces, affecting defense contractors and military service providers whose operations depend on authorized military engagements."}],"method":"llm","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","inputHash":"dfa2d0b90a01d4e707be048b","classifiedAt":"2026-07-30T02:35:36.324Z"},"plain":{"whatItDoes":"This joint resolution would order the President to remove U.S. Armed Forces from hostilities within or against Iran unless a declaration of war or authorization to use military force for such purpose has been enacted.","whoItTouches":"Mostly people outside the United States. It reaches most readers here only indirectly.","everydayEffect":"If it passed, the change would show up in what the United States does abroad. Nothing has changed yet. Most bills never become law.","confidence":"crs-summary","source":"Reworded from the official summary. Staff at the Congressional Research Service wrote that summary. It is public domain, and the full text of it is further down this page.","titleInPlainWords":null},"overlaps":[{"billId":"119-sjres-115","bioguideId":"K000384","cycle":2026,"score":0.012127935407586254,"matches":[{"industry":"defense","donorAmount":6000,"donorShare":0.012127935407586254,"billConfidence":0.85,"contribution":0.012127935407586254}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.8066099633131976},"member":{"name":"Tim Kaine","chamber":"Senate","state":"VA","imageUrl":"data/portraits/K000384.jpg","role":"Cosponsor"},"donorProfile":{"bioguideId":"K000384","cycle":2026,"totalItemized":494725.58999999997,"byIndustry":[{"industry":"health-providers","amount":15500,"share":0.03133049980293116,"contributionCount":5},{"industry":"legal","amount":15100,"share":0.03052197077575874,"contributionCount":13},{"industry":"pharma","amount":13500,"share":0.027287854667069074,"contributi